WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.970 --> 00:00:04.920
- Narrator: Odds are you are
surrounded by nose-pickers.

00:00:04.920 --> 00:00:09.280
It's true, one study found
that 91% of adults admitted

00:00:09.280 --> 00:00:11.340
to picking their nose regularly.

00:00:11.340 --> 00:00:14.120
So chances are you've probably mined

00:00:14.120 --> 00:00:17.060
for some juicy nose nuggets yourself.

00:00:17.060 --> 00:00:19.260
But maybe you didn't stop there.

00:00:19.260 --> 00:00:24.010
Maybe you ate those boogers, too.

00:00:24.010 --> 00:00:27.430
And it turns out that
slimy snack could hurt more

00:00:27.430 --> 00:00:30.013
than just your social standing.

00:00:32.090 --> 00:00:34.750
Let's take a closer look
at that booger, shall we?

00:00:34.750 --> 00:00:36.470
It's mostly made out of water,

00:00:36.470 --> 00:00:40.040
gel-like proteins that give
it that gooey consistency,

00:00:40.040 --> 00:00:43.930
and special immune proteins
that fight off germs.

00:00:43.930 --> 00:00:46.970
Those immune proteins
are especially useful,

00:00:46.970 --> 00:00:48.780
because boogers are teeming

00:00:48.780 --> 00:00:52.010
with harmful viruses like influenza.

00:00:52.010 --> 00:00:54.930
And actually that's the whole point.

00:00:54.930 --> 00:00:57.780
Boogers serve as your
body's frontline defense

00:00:57.780 --> 00:01:00.200
against invading germs.

00:01:00.200 --> 00:01:03.440
When you breathe in, you're
not just inhaling air.

00:01:03.440 --> 00:01:08.320
You're also taking in
bacteria, viruses and dirt.

00:01:08.320 --> 00:01:11.750
All those nasty things
get trapped by a layer

00:01:11.750 --> 00:01:15.160
of sticky snot that line your nostrils.

00:01:15.160 --> 00:01:17.860
It's like flypaper for the flu.

00:01:17.860 --> 00:01:19.930
And as you continue to breathe,

00:01:19.930 --> 00:01:23.350
air hardens the mucus into a solid booger,

00:01:23.350 --> 00:01:27.880
a gooey prison cell for
all your ensnared enemies.

00:01:27.880 --> 00:01:31.430
Now normally you can get rid
of that bacteria-ridden ball

00:01:31.430 --> 00:01:34.970
either when you sneeze or blow your nose.

00:01:34.970 --> 00:01:38.650
But if you for some reason
decide to eat it instead,

00:01:38.650 --> 00:01:40.930
it stands to reason that
you're putting yourself

00:01:40.930 --> 00:01:42.680
at risk of infection,

00:01:42.680 --> 00:01:45.300
because as your body digests the booger,

00:01:45.300 --> 00:01:49.860
it can release those harmful
pathogens into your system.

00:01:49.860 --> 00:01:52.430
Now some people claim
that eating your boogers

00:01:52.430 --> 00:01:56.030
can strengthen your immune
system by training your body

00:01:56.030 --> 00:01:59.640
to recognize and attack invading microbes.

00:01:59.640 --> 00:02:03.500
But sorry to say, there is
zero scientific evidence

00:02:03.500 --> 00:02:05.240
to support any health benefits

00:02:05.240 --> 00:02:08.190
from eating your boogers, zero, zilch.

00:02:08.190 --> 00:02:10.880
And besides whether or not
you decide to eat them,

00:02:10.880 --> 00:02:14.940
just getting a hold of your
boogers can be dangerous.

00:02:14.940 --> 00:02:17.640
For example, scratching
up the inside of your nose

00:02:17.640 --> 00:02:20.580
opens the door for a nasty bacteria

00:02:20.580 --> 00:02:22.950
that lurks under your fingernails,

00:02:22.950 --> 00:02:26.230
Staphylococcus aureus, or staph.

00:02:26.230 --> 00:02:29.820
A 2006 study found that
nose-pickers were more likely

00:02:29.820 --> 00:02:33.850
to have staph in their nose
than those who abstain.

00:02:33.850 --> 00:02:35.350
And that's a big problem,

00:02:35.350 --> 00:02:38.570
since staph can cause serious abscesses,

00:02:38.570 --> 00:02:43.570
or pus-filled pockets inside
your nose and on your face.

00:02:44.740 --> 00:02:47.300
Even worse, if you keep picking,

00:02:47.300 --> 00:02:49.900
you could actually puncture your septum.

00:02:49.900 --> 00:02:52.100
In one case, a 53 year old woman

00:02:52.100 --> 00:02:56.070
managed to carve a hole
right through her sinus.

00:02:56.070 --> 00:02:58.950
And if that sinus becomes
infected badly enough,

00:02:58.950 --> 00:03:02.980
it can erode your skull,
leaving the door open

00:03:02.980 --> 00:03:06.733
for bacteria to march
right into your brain.

00:03:07.640 --> 00:03:11.290
But to be fair, these
are extreme scenarios.

00:03:11.290 --> 00:03:13.570
One time probably won't hurt you,

00:03:13.570 --> 00:03:16.810
but when it comes down to it,
next time you feel the urge

00:03:16.810 --> 00:03:21.063
to mine for green gold,
just grab a tissue, man.

00:03:22.504 --> 00:03:23.908
(blows nose)

